Theorem RL-20: PotentiallyShared requires a shared-safe capability

  Preconditions:
    - ThreadReachability has been frozen by RL-19.
    - A physical planner advertises ThreadCapability.

  Soundness property:
    Forall thread fact T and capability C:

      (P1) potentiallyShared is covered only by sharedSafe.

      (P2) confined is covered by confinedOnly or sharedSafe.

    The theorem defines an admission relation, not one mandatory physical
    synchronization implementation.

  Proof obligation:
    Exhaustive ThreadReachability x ThreadCapability case analysis.

    Part (P1/P2) - capability grid:
      potentiallyShared + confinedOnly -> false
      potentiallyShared + sharedSafe -> true
      confined + confinedOnly -> true
      confined + sharedSafe -> true
      Coverage gate: 4 capability cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY - section_08::verify_rl20_thread_capability;
        potentially_shared_requires_safe_capability)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)
      refinement (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-20 because potentiallyShared requires sharedSafe while confined admits either physical capability
